module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.protect_carve_out_reopens_the_protected_subject

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data protect_carve_out_reopens_the_protected_subject: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "protect_carve_out_reopens_the_protected_subject" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a confinement that names a refused write (ProtectSystem=strict, ProtectHome=read-only) carves the protected subject back in as a writable path, so the write succeeds. DISTINGUISHING FACT: the annotation and the Protect* properties can both be true while ReadWritePaths (or an equivalent exception) is a parent of the thing they claim to refuse. HARM: a dispatched worker with --dangerously-skip-permissions writes the deployed binary or tree; the recovery cost is a dirty release, paid later at interest. Silent success is below the ladder.",

    "SPECIMEN (smart-gull-336 item c, operator plan 2026-10-13): gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dispatch_actuator dispatch_worker_writable_paths yielded ReadWritePaths=/opt/gunbc on srv1_live_dashboard_instance (instance_root=/opt/gunbc), covering /opt/gunbc/bin and /opt/gunbc/gunbc. The module claimed a refused write; on srv1 that claim did not hold.",

    "REPAIR: the writable set is this attempt's working_directory, the directory that holds its stdout log, and repo/.git (the common git dir a linked worktree commit/stash/fetch writes). Not instance_root, not the whole worktree root, not the whole attempt-state root, not the exit spool. dispatch_worker_path_is_writable is the membership fold.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable — the kernel would refuse the write if the carve-out were narrower; with the wide carve-out the invalid write is a silent success. After this change, mechanically preventable: test.claim.roadmap.dispatch_worker_confinement_witness the_srv1_worker_cannot_write_the_deployed_binary_or_tree is the discriminating dry RED (writable=/opt/gunbc covers bin on main; after the derivation it does not). The wet systemd-run probe is test.claim.roadmap.dispatch_worker_writable_sandbox_wet_witness, OfflineLocalRecipe, because it needs a user systemd manager and the live /opt/gunbc layout.",

    "CEILING: mechanically preventable while writable paths are a joined string the author can still spell as instance_root. Structurally guaranteed once a typed AttemptResourceSet (or equivalent) has no constructor for the deploy tree or binary. Outside the modeled guarantee: systemd's own enforcement, which remains a kernel/manager fact. NEXT TRIGGER: consume Manager B's AttemptResourceSet so the deploy tree has no constructor in the worker writable set.",

    "CONSUMPTION: this per-class record joins the derived gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster recurring_failure_mode_roster.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dispatch_actuator", decl_name: "dispatch_worker_writable_paths"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dispatch_actuator", decl_name: "dispatch_worker_path_is_writable"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.roadmap.dispatch_worker_confinement_witness", decl_name: "the_srv1_worker_cannot_write_the_deployed_binary_or_tree"),
  ],
}
